WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.274
Hi, I'm Quince!

00:00:02.274 --> 00:00:04.241
AgentJev picks between an agent's options.

00:00:04.241 --> 00:00:08.831
Here's how it ignores the order of the list, yet lets the options talk.

00:00:10.642 --> 00:00:14.313
Encode the shared state once, give every option a private branch, then

00:00:14.313 --> 00:00:18.596
let the options meet, but only in a small head that has no positions.

00:00:20.342 --> 00:00:23.910
The state and the question are encoded once and cached.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:27.835
On a sixty-four-option request, that removes ninety-two point four percent of

00:00:27.835 --> 00:00:29.262
the backbone's input tokens.

00:00:29.682 --> 00:00:32.443
Each option gets its own copy of that cache.

00:00:32.443 --> 00:00:36.124
No option sees another, and every one starts at the same position.

00:00:36.544 --> 00:00:38.909
Each branch comes out as one vector.

00:00:38.909 --> 00:00:43.639
Only now do the options meet, in a two-layer transformer with no positional embeddings.

00:00:44.059 --> 00:00:46.372
A scorer reads one number per option.

00:00:46.372 --> 00:00:49.346
Nothing anywhere records which slot an option arrived in.

00:00:50.692 --> 00:00:54.293
The set head's output is added back onto each option's own vector.

00:00:54.713 --> 00:00:56.911
The first term is each option, read alone.

00:00:57.759 --> 00:01:00.221
The second is what knowing the rest of the set adds.

00:01:01.195 --> 00:01:04.814
Zero that second term, and you are back to a plain per-option scorer.

00:01:06.192 --> 00:01:10.427
Shuffle the list: across two thousand five hundred and twenty permutations, no

00:01:10.427 --> 00:01:14.310
answer changed, and no logit moved past the float's last bits.

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:18.219
Change which other options are on it, and a logit moves by

00:01:18.219 --> 00:01:20.545
a median of zero point zero eight eight.

00:01:20.545 --> 00:01:21.708
The options do interact.

00:01:23.142 --> 00:01:27.340
Isolate options in the backbone, let them meet in a head without

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:29.789
positions: order carries nothing, content still counts.

00:01:31.692 --> 00:01:35.504
To recap: a shared prefix, private branches, and a head where

00:01:35.504 --> 00:01:36.890
options meet without positions.

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:39.420
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:40.022
I'm Quince.

00:01:40.022 --> 00:01:40.324
Bye!
